in the comments and I’ll include them in

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.960
the video. I’ll also be doing a detailed
breakdown of the episode either tomorrow or

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:38.960
friday.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.980
So where to start, so many things to talk
about but, here are my top 5 favorite moments.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:45.830
Number 5 - Sherlock and mycroft. Throughout
the episode sherlock and mycroft have a number

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:51.160
of scenes that really turn the dial on mock
resentment and anger up to 11. You also get

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.580
the sense that if Sherlock were ever to be
incapacitated, Mycroft could do what he does

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:55.580
just as easily.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:01.320
Mycroft’s skills as a detective become a
big part of the comedy of the episode and

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.190
it was hilarious to watch the two of them
dance around each other.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:16.479
4 - The 
fan theories addressed. All of the sherlock

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:23.359
lives theories were filmed and presented in
the most hilarious possible ways. Mark Gatiss

00:01:23.359 --> 00:01:26.979
and Steven Moffat essentially winked from
behind the camera every time we saw a new

00:01:26.979 --> 00:01:29.770
theory play out.

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:34.330
I don’t think they’ll ever explicitly
state which scenario was the correct one.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:39.159
Meaning that there’s elements of truth to
every one of the theories you see during the

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:40.159
episode.

00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:41.859
I did a video of my own about which theory
I think is the best, but my favorite one during

00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:44.540
the episode was the sherlock fan club one.
WTF.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.039
3 - the mind palace. Sherlock uses the mind
palace all the time, but you mostly just see

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:52.240
it during hound of baskerville in season 2.
I really liked the way they turned it into

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:53.960
a joke in this episode.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:57.749
To be clear he uses it several times, but
I’m talking about the joke that’s made

00:01:57.749 --> 00:01:58.840
about it near the end.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:04.060
They also updated a lot of the way they show
the mind palace visually and show you much

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:09.170
more of what sherlock is imagining in his
head. I thought it was unnecessary, but I

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:14.349
can understand how they want to literally
show us how hyperkinetic his mind is.

00:02:14.349 --> 00:02:24.159
2 - the new characters. We get to meet Mary
Morstan which was so much fun. I almost liked

00:02:24.159 --> 00:02:28.049
sherlock scanning her more than I liked him
trying to scan Irene Adler in scandal.

00:02:28.049 --> 00:02:32.580
She’s not a huge part of this episode, but
the wedding will be a big part of episode

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.849
2, so we’ll get a chance to learn more about
her on sunday.

00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:39.230
The other new character is the villain charles
augustus magnussen. I liked the way the episode

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:43.469
teased him like it teased moriarty at the
end of study in pink. But I didn’t think

00:02:43.469 --> 00:02:48.879
we should have seen him. Just a minor complaint.
I liked how we didn’t see moriarty until

00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:49.879
great game.

00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:56.459
I think they just wanted to put a face on
the villain this soon just to speed up the

00:02:56.459 --> 00:03:00.440
narrative. Because they went a whole episode
last season without using moriarty which a

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:04.810
lot of people felt was a waste.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:09.080
1 - sherlock and watson reunion. It had been
implied for a long time that by the end of

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:14.159
this episode all of the core relationships
would be restored, but the fun part was watching

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:17.670
the johnlock reunion play out over the course
of the episode.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:21.810
All I could think when sherlock first revealed
himself to watson was that scene during scandal

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:25.640
where watson is punching and throttling sherlock
on the ground.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:30.219
It’s like sherlock is looking at watson
and he’s staring death in the face right

00:03:30.219 --> 00:03:31.230
and he just can’t see it.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:35.849
I just crept to the edge of my seat and sure
enough the music swells up and watson leaps

00:03:35.849 --> 00:03:38.430
at him as the camera goes into slow motion.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:45.370
There were so many moments to talk about,
but since I don’t want to spoil too much

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.019
I’ll save a lot of that for my breakdown
of the episode tomorrow.

00:03:48.019 --> 00:03:53.209
Let me know what you’re favorite moment
was whether it was the reunion or all the

00:03:53.209 --> 00:03:54.909
jokes about the sherlock lives theories.

00:03:54.909 --> 00:04:00.361
Here’s my review. Overall I thought it was
perfect with a few exceptions. Just like a

00:04:00.361 --> 00:04:06.430
study in pink, The real task of this episode
was to form or re form Team Sherlock and it

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:11.609
did that perfectly. I was amazed at the lengths
Steven Moffat and Mark Gatiss went to to address

00:04:11.609 --> 00:04:13.040
all of the fans questions.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:18.310
The quite literally filmed almost every major
sherlock lives theory and then made fun of

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:22.290
themselves in the most hilarious ways. One
of the things that makes sherlock so great

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:26.630
is the wordplay and while benedict cumberbatch,
martin freeman and the other actors are largely

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:31.330
responsible for the interpretation of those
jokes. It’s really Mark Gatiss who deserves

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.330
the credit for writing such witty and funny
dialogue.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.260
He was the only credited writer on the episode,
so he deserves the first high five. After

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:40.510
that it’s all cumberbatch and freeman. Not
to leave out the rest of the cast, Amanda

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:43.240
Abbigngton is a very welcome addition to team
sherlock.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.240
I’ll talk more about the details of the
three’s company situation that’s going

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.250
on right now between them tomorrow, but needless
to say she will be a formidable opponent to

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:48.180
sherlock over watson’s affections.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.160
The sheer amount of fan service that the episode
performed was amazing and I loved that they

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:56.200
were able to do that for us without it seeming
too ridiculous. One of the things I’ve always

00:04:56.200 --> 00:05:00.780
liked about the show is how playful it allows
everyone to be without the actors stepping

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.800
out of character.

